  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Find the exact value of the radius $r$ and angle $\\theta$ of the sector that has an",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "area of $100\\text{ cm}^2$ and arc length of $20\\text{ cm}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$r=10\\text{ cm},\\quad \\theta=2\\text{ radians}$.",
          "worked": "Using $l=r\\theta$ and $A=\\frac{1}{2}r^2\\theta$, we have $A=\\frac{1}{2}rl$.\n$$\\begin{align*}r&=\\frac{2A}{l}\\\\r&=\\frac{2(100)}{20}\\\\r&=10\\text{ cm}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{l}{r}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{20}{10}\\\\\\theta&=2\\text{ radians}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "area of $\\pi\\text{ cm}^2$ and arc length of $\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\text{ cm}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$r=4\\text{ cm},\\quad \\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\text{ radians}$.",
          "worked": "Using $A=\\frac{1}{2}rl$ and $l=r\\theta$:\n$$\\begin{align*}r&=\\frac{2A}{l}\\\\r&=\\frac{2\\pi}{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\\\r&=4\\text{ cm}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{l}{r}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{4}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\text{ radians}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      }
    ]
  },
